  "content": "The initial bricklaying phase of the campaign concluded a month later. On Nov. 12, 2025, the attacker or attackers set up a command-and-control (C2) channel via Dropbox, so that their malicious exfiltrations might appear like legitimate network traffic. They registered a new scheduled task for running batch files, branded as an ordinary Lenovo system health check — the Lenovo bit demonstrating an intimate knowledge of their target's machine — and then deployed a custom infostealer.",
